
README_3DPBL

Compiling WRF with 3DPBL parameterization on kestrel (09/06/2024)

To use WRF with the most recent version of the 3DPBL scheme use git as follows:

% git clone https://github.com/twjuliano/WRF.git

You can list all the remote branches in this repository as follows:

% cd WRF
% git branch -r

Then you can checkout the 3DPBL develop branch to your local repository as follows:

% git checkout -b develop_3dpbl_on_top origin/develop_3dpbl_on_top

Make sure that the develop_3dpbl_on_top is the active branch by issuing the command:

% git branch

The active branch will be denoted with a '*' infront of the name.

After making sure that the correct branch is active modify Registry.EM_COMMON so
that the line that defines package lesscheme looks like this:

package   lesscheme      bl_pbl_physics==0           -             scalar:qke_adv;state:qke,tke_pbl,sh3d,tsq,qsq,cov,el_pbl

Also comment out the lines in share/module_check_a_mundo.F checking for combining LESscheme and MYNNPBLSCHEME2(3) and EEPSSCHEME with LESschem as follows:

