This will enable combining a PBL scheme that includes a prognostic equation for TKE on the outer domain with the LES or the 3DPBL scheme on the inner domain.

After making modifications to the registry load the following modules and export 
variables listed below.
Create a shell script (e.g. loadm.sh) using the example bleow.

#------------ cut here
#!/bin/bash

module --force purge
module load anaconda3
module load craype-x86-spr
module load PrgEnv-intel
module load perftools-base/22.12.0
module load netcdf/4.9.2-intel-oneapi-mpi-intel
module load hdf5/1.14.1-2-intel-oneapi-mpi-intel
module load pnetcdf/1.12.2-intel
module load intel-oneapi-mkl/2023.2.0-intel
export OMP_NUM_THREADS=1
export NETCDF=/nopt/nrel/apps/libraries/08-23/spack/opt/spack/linux-rhel8-icelake/intel-2021.10.0/netcdf
export PATH="/nopt/nrel/apps/software/wrf/intel/installs/wps_dep_libs/bin":$PATH
export WRF_EM_CORE=1

module list
#------------ cut here

Load modules and define variables by executing the loadm.sh script as follows:
% . ./loadm.sh

After loading modules and defining variables check Makefile in the main (WRF) directory.
If the Makefile includes the following nc4_test lines:

## rule used by configure to test if this will compile with netcdf4
#nc4_test:
#       if [ $(USENETCDFPAR) -eq 0 ] ; then \
#        ( cd tools ; /bin/rm -f nc4_test.{exe,nc,o} ; $(SCC) -o nc4_test.exe nc4_test.c -I$(NETCDF)/include -L$(NETCDF)/lib -lnetcdf $(NETCDF4_DEP_LIB) ; cd .. ) ; \
#       else \
#        ( cd tools ; /bin/rm -f nc4_test.{exe,nc,o} ; $(DM_CC) -o nc4_test.exe nc4_test.c -I$(NETCDF)/include -L$(NETCDF)/lib -lnetcdf $(NETCDF4_DEP_LIB) ; cd ..  ) ; \
#       fi

Comment these lines out and add the following line instead

nc4_test:
	@cd tools ; /bin/rm -f nc4_test.{exe,nc,o} ; $(SCC) -o nc4_test.exe nc4_test.c -I$(NETCDF)/include -L$(NETCDF)/lib $(USENETCDF) ; cd ..

Notice that there is a <tab> before @cd and not blank spaces.
This is necessary to avoid an error when configuring WRF and creating configure.wrf file.
With this modification it will not be possible to use parallel netcdf output option.

Configure WRF compilation by running 
% ./configure
and selecting option 
15. (dmpar) INTEL

Then modify configure.wrf by commenting out the existing DEP_LIB_PATH variable definition and
add the new definition shown below. 
This makes sure that the correct hdf library path and mkl library path are defined. The library mkl is intel math library required by 3DPBL for solving systems of linear equations using LU decomposition (based on LAPACK library).


#DEP_LIB_PATH    = -L/nopt/nrel/apps/libraries/08-23/spack/opt/spack/linux-rhel8-icelake/intel-2021.10.0/netcdf-fortran-4.6.0-2ptt3qnjy5vtg5s4fvo7l5qyjomufnrt/lib

DEP_LIB_PATH    = -L/nopt/nrel/apps/libraries/08-23/spack/opt/spack/linux-rhel8-icelake/intel-2021.10.0/netcdf-c-4.9.2-twcnffnqrckvlwqn7udxatwmyf26r6es/lib -lnetcdf -L/nopt/nrel/apps/libraries/08-23/spack/opt/spack/linux-rhel8-icelake/intel-2021.10.0/netcdf-fortran-4.6.0-2ptt3qnjy5vtg5s4fvo7l5qyjomufnrt/lib -lnetcdff -lnetcdf -lnetcdf -lm 

Add the following line under definition of LIB_BUNDLED as follows:

LIB_MKL         = -L/nopt/nrel/apps/libraries/08-23/spack/opt/spack/linux-rhel8-icelake/intel-2021.10.0/hdf5-1.14.1-2-x43jlkan4ddpbd3hq7rzntsdmrq4qery/lib -L/nopt/nrel/apps/cpu_stack/libraries-intel/06-24/linux-rhel8-sapphirerapids/oneapi-2024.1.0/intel-oneapi-mkl-2023.2.0-cxkmsrntwshafhfoubnmiimvx6mn7ofl/lib/intel64 -Wl,--no-as-needed -lmkl_intel_lp64 -lmkl_sequential -lmkl_core -lm

and then add $(LIB_MKL) to the definition of LIB as follows:

LIB             =    $(LIB_BUNDLED) $(LIB_EXTERNAL) $(LIB_LOCAL) $(LIB_MKL) $(LIB_WRF_HYDRO)
